#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:411
msgid ""
"We won't create a subscriber in this tutorial, but you can try to write one "
"yourself for practice (use :doc:`Writing-A-Simple-Cpp-Publisher-And-"
"Subscriber` to help)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:414
msgid "5 (Extra) Use an existing interface definition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:418
msgid ""
"You can use an existing interface definition in a new interface definition. "
"For example, let's say there is a message named ``Contact.msg`` that belongs "
"to an existing ROS 2 package named ``rosidl_tutorials_msgs``. Assume that "
"its definition is identical to our custom-made ``AddressBook.msg`` interface "
"from earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:422
msgid ""
"In that case you could have defined ``AddressBook.msg`` (an interface in the "
"package *with* your nodes) as type ``Contact`` (an interface in a *separate* "
"package). You could even define ``AddressBook.msg`` as an *array* of type "
"``Contact``, like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:427
msgid "rosidl_tutorials_msgs/Contact[] address_book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:429
msgid ""
"To generate this message you would need to declare a dependency on ``Contact."
"msg's`` package, ``rosidl_tutorials_msgs``, in ``package.xml``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:431
msgid ""
"<build_depend>rosidl_tutorials_msgs</build_depend>\n"
"\n"
"<exec_depend>rosidl_tutorials_msgs</exec_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:437
msgid "And in ``CMakeLists.txt``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:439
msgid ""
"find_package(rosidl_tutorials_msgs REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"rosidl_generate_interfaces(${PROJECT_NAME}\n"
"  ${msg_files}\n"
"  DEPENDENCIES rosidl_tutorials_msgs\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:448
msgid ""
"You would also need to include the header of ``Contact.msg`` in your "
"publisher node in order to be able to add ``contacts`` to your "
"``address_book``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:450
msgid "#include \"rosidl_tutorials_msgs/msg/contact.hpp\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:454
msgid "You could change the callback to something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:456
msgid ""
"auto publish_msg = [this]() -> void {\n"
"   auto msg = std::make_shared<more_interfaces::msg::AddressBook>();\n"
"   {\n"
"     rosidl_tutorials_msgs::msg::Contact contact;\n"
"     contact.first_name = \"John\";\n"
"     contact.last_name = \"Doe\";\n"
"     contact.phone_number = \"1234567890\";\n"
"     contact.phone_type = contact.PHONE_TYPE_MOBILE;\n"
"     msg->address_book.push_back(contact);\n"
"   }\n"
"   {\n"
"     rosidl_tutorials_msgs::msg::Contact contact;\n"
"     contact.first_name = \"Jane\";\n"
"     contact.last_name = \"Doe\";\n"
"     contact.phone_number = \"4254242424\";\n"
"     contact.phone_type = contact.PHONE_TYPE_HOME;\n"
"     msg->address_book.push_back(contact);\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   std::cout << \"Publishing address book:\" << std::endl;\n"
"   for (auto contact : msg->address_book) {\n"
"     std::cout << \"First:\" << contact.first_name << \"  Last:\" << contact."
"last_name <<\n"
"       std::endl;\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   address_book_publisher_->publish(*msg);\n"
" };"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:486
msgid ""
"Building and running these changes would show the msg defined as expected, "
"as well as the array of msgs defined above."
msgstr ""

